e text is after gone fishing???\nImage\nGordo [VICE],  — 1:11 PM\nis showing that doing gear up is required to receive it \nwhich is the same mistake that i have done on mine\nGogsi123 — 1:12 PM\nchat I don't think the map viewr is working correctly :xdd:\nImage\nI only have the water\nGordo [VICE],  — 1:12 PM\n🤣\nZkhan4509 — 1:12 PM\nLol\n [VICE], \nZkhan4509 — 1:13 PM\nI told it to build on your chart and make its own charts as well, I can send the one it made on its own but I trusted this more cause I assume you'd have check yours\nGordo [VICE],  — 1:13 PM\ninteresting\nranveer [COYS],  — 1:14 PM\n [VICE], \nZkhan4509 — 1:16 PM\nYeah\nZkhan4509 — 1:21 PM\nAnyways ^\nranveer [COYS],  — 1:24 PM\nlet it rip\nGogsi123 — 3:26 PM\nshoutout to Rockstar for finally making a decent map organization system\nthe map is split into 1km x 1km tiles and they are labeled (n|s)x_(e|w)y based on where they are of 0,0. \n\nSo for example this tile is one east, one north of 0,0, so it's n01_e01.ymap\nImage\nGogsi123 — 3:42 PM\nok so I think loot is global per model of container. That is the same crate in different places on the map will give the same loot\nfor example the crate that @Gordo sent has one slot for a large item and two slots for medium loot\nImage\nnow how that loot is determined I don't know yet. There is a file called container_crate.ymt which is probably responsible but CodeX can't decode it yet\nI'll throw it at Claude and see if it comes up with anything\nthese are probably all responsible for loot, yeah\nImage\nZkhan4509 — 3:48 PM\nThat's actually very good\nSo 0,0 is its own tile?\nGogsi123 — 4:03 PM\nok each map zone seems to have a type (industrial, construction, military, farm, etc) and the loot table in the container_crates.ymt depends on that. Claude is cooking\nImage\nGordo [VICE],  — 4:11 PM\ndammit, so is really rng\ni guess this is one way to make gameplay interesting\nbut sad for mission skips, since i need a consistent way of getting C4s\nthis information about each crate having different itens depending on the zone is actually interesting, i might turn it into a fact for viper facts and glitches \nunnamed found a RPG in the map, but because is a primary weapon it can get removed from the inventory at the first mission, just because R* \nGordo [VICE],  — 4:24 PM\nlet me know when the tool is capable of finding something on the map, to help search this thing\n [VICE], \nZkhan4509 — 4:35 PM\nBro is gonna steal Claude's work (/j)\nGordo [VICE],  — 4:35 PM\nmore like, credit gogsi for paying claude to do it \nlol\nGogsi123 — 4:37 PM\ncredit my employer for paying for my Claude subscription instead of raising my salary\nGordo [VICE],  — 4:39 PM\nlet me guess, he got the most expensive version of claude instead of just increasing your salary, which would been cheaper to do?\nbecause this seems to be a common occurrence from what i have been seeing lately in the industry 🤣 \nZkhan4509 — 4:40 PM\nYou're allowed to use Claude for personal use as well?\nLucky\nGogsi123 — 4:41 PM\nI mean they didn't say if we are allowed so I assumed we are :xdd:\n [VICE], \nZkhan4509 — 4:41 PM\nMy employer pays for openAI enterprise and I have access to daybreak aswell since my employer is certified for it\nZkhan4509 — 4:42 PM\nI am not since my employer is strict in these things like, it's a federal crime to use company property for personal use\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-25T17:46:15-05:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\n<USER_SETTINGS_CHANGE>\nThe user changed setting `Model Selection` from Gemini 3.8 Flash (High) to Gemini 4 Hydrogen (High). No need to comment on this change if the user doesn't ask about it. If reporting what model you are, please use a human readable name instead of the exact string.\n</USER_SETTINGS_CHANGE>"}
